# L §2.3 MODE, §8.3 LOAD-UNIT (tally 2.1.6, issue #79): a converted flows whose mode is day, a date, not a rounding
# code, is refused LOAD-UNIT `flows: the mode is date, not a rounding code`, the engine's bytes. tally 2.1.5's
# refcore built the message from the call's name, which a flows node lacks, and crashed (REFCORE-NOT-YET).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

input fx: num PLN/EUR

input day: date

input eamt: money EUR

place konto: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount eamt

ask b: flows(konto, 2026-01) in PLN at fx day law 2026-01-01

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  fx = 4.3333
  day = 2026-02-10
  eamt = 1.00 EUR
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT flows: the mode is date, not a rounding code (m.tally:28)
